  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Supporting core Displacement Tracking Matrix activities in the SudanSupporting core Displacement Tracking Matrix activities in the Sudan</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Sudan has become the largest displacement crisis globally, with over 15 million people displaced internally or across borders to neighbouring countries. Nearly one-third of the population has been displaced, with internally displaced persons (IDPs) recorded in 10,000 locations in 185 localities across all 18 states. The humanitarian situation is critical, marked by extreme food insecurity and malnutrition, major disease outbreaks, and urgent shelter needs.To guide critical interventions and strategies towards the most affected populations and areas across Sudan, and optimize limited resource allocations, IOM-DTM proposes implementing regular data collection to provide statistically representative data on access to services, living conditions, and priority needs across various population groups, including but not limited to IDPs and returnees.</narrative>
  </description>
